1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,410
That wet dog shake is a feat of physics.

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:06,370
A soaked Labrador can carry about a pound of water in its fur.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:10,650
Drying that with body heat would burn about a fifth of its daily food.

4
00:00:10,850 --> 00:00:12,330
So instead, it shakes.

5
00:00:12,810 --> 00:00:15,700
It twists back and forth about four times a second,

6
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:18,210
starting at the head and rippling down to the tail.

7
00:00:18,530 --> 00:00:20,900
Its loose skin whips around even further,

8
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:22,790
flinging the water off faster.

9
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:26,510
In about four seconds, seventy percent of the water is gone.

10
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:28,880
Smaller animals have to shake faster.

11
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:31,630
A mouse does it thirty times a second.

12
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,840
So when your dog climbs out of the bath,

13
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:35,033
grab a towel, because
